  "summaries": [
    {
      "id": "sum-8ae77b",
      "kind": "overview",
      "body": "narfbg asked ASVS to address homoglyph and visual-deception attacks after a Wiz write-up of malicious OAuth app names. tghosth first argued that V1.1.1, V1.5.3 and V2.2.1 already form a canonicalize-then-validate pipeline. narfbg replied that mixed-script names are an attack on human cognition, not parsers, and that V2.2.1 is only an incidental home. The thread then drafted a dedicated control for unique authoritative names, rejected the word 'script' as colliding with executable code, and settled on 'writing system' plus section-level guidance citing Unicode TR #39. elarlang placed the likely home in V2.2. No text has been merged. jmanico's first comment was later edited.",
      "citations": [
        {
          "type": "issue_comment",
          "url": "https://github.com/OWASP/ASVS/issues/3338#issuecomment-3945416469",
          "issue": 3338,
